            "author_association": "CONTRIBUTOR",
            "body": "> I personally prefer this current solution.\r\n\r\nFor a case like:\r\n```\r\nsrc/nvim/normal.c|106 col 3| error: unknown type name ‘nt’; did you mean ‘int’?\r\n||   106 |   nt mapped_len;\r\n||       |   ^~\r\n||       |   int\r\nsrc/nvim/normal.c|108 col 3| error: unknown type name ‘nt’; did you mean ‘int’?\r\n||   108 |   nt idx;\r\n||       |   ^~\r\n||       |   int\r\n```\r\n\r\nThe current implementation appends 8 diagnostics, but it should append only 2, with the lines merged after each.\r\n\r\n> However, imo the second parameter should be an optional opts table.\r\n\r\nAgree.\r\n\r\n> Should I keep the current solution or should I rewrite it to how the reviewer wanted it to be?\r\n\r\nCurrently, it produces incorrect output, as explained above. I suggest writing a test for this - it will help ensure the expected behavior is achieved.\r\n\r\n> Also can someone pls tell me why my checks are failing 😭\r\n\r\n- The docs test is failing because you changed a public function signature but did not regenerate help files. Run `make doc` and commit the changes.\r\n\r\n- lintcommit fails because your commit message is too long.\r\n\r\n- the remaining test failures are just flaky.",
